    rdf:value """the Torre di Gallo. So I went to see it, and took Herbert Horne with me. We found a terribly ruined but still fine Pollaiuolo. We had a pleasant moonlight walk after dinner. 
Tuesday Nov. 9. 1897. Villa Rosa. Fiesole. 
In the morning I wrote to Wilfrid Blaydes, who is at Siena, telling him I had told Bernhard all our story. In the afternoon we went, with Janet Dodge, to the new Villas, and Miss Blood and Horne met us, and we consulted about furnishings. Horne came to dinner and stayed late, looking over photographs, and telling us of his scheme for a new and """^^xsd:string ;
